Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): preserve archive fallback scope and release ACK
 promptly [daveey]

Follow up independent review of PR4013 at f61509f5cd8505c75fd67c9f2a81e4e80aa61536 before landing.

Why did the ownerless archive target default instead of active work? Owner capture pinned primary before profile resolution, and a swallowed resolution transport error yielded undefined; the later pinned write defaulted it. Why was it missed? The prior regression covered successful resolution to work, not unlisted/unresolved fallback. Capture the invocation profile before awaiting resolution; use it only after existing ambiguous-listed refusal, and carry the same profile through safety checks and PATCH. Explicit row profiles still win.

Why could a successful archive look pending for another six seconds? Authoritative diagnostic GET was awaited before onArchived and hidden.end. Why not caught? ACK/verification tests resolved the read immediately. Detach the diagnostic with handled rejection; it cannot restore or resend a committed write. Pending-read regression checks success before rejecting the read.

Why did five review mutations survive? Tests covered positive replay but omitted settled queue cleanup, ownerless primary switches, remaining deadline cap, late settled success and wrong-id archived verification. Add direct negative assertions for all five; all mutants now killed.

Proof on worker-a1, disposable deps tree at exact reviewed source: final new regressions RED (2 failures,40 pass); corrected source GREEN229 tests across seven modules including actual useSessionActions callers; TypeScript noEmit and ESLint pass; scripts/check21 pass. Mutants baseline15 pass,5/5 killed. Independent precommit read-only review approves current four-file diff. Fresh published-head CI and independent review still required. laptop-1 passive acceptance remains UNPROVEN; no launch/fault injection performed.
